Carafe Lab: the control channel presses keys inside Eden: `press <ms> <key>...` holds the keys, named as Qt names
them (`C`, `Up`, `Return`), for the given milliseconds and lets them go. The presses reach Eden's keyboard input
the way a key of the window does, without the X server or the window's focus. Eden answers `pressed <keys>`, then
`released`; `error idle` when no software runs.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

diff --git a/src/yuzu/main_window.cpp b/src/yuzu/main_window.cpp
